00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:45.070
And so when I had the idea for this movie, I did this thing where I brought him in really
所以当我有了这部电影的想法时，我做了一件事，就是很早就把他们带进来，

163
00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.770
early and I pitched them the idea.
向他们推销了这个想法。

164
00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.610
And then I started telling them about the characters as I thought of them.
然后我开始向他们讲述我构思的角色。

165
00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.190
And I showed them the early drawings.
我还给他们看了早期的草图。

166
00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.750
And then as artist drawings started coming in, I showed them.
随着艺术家的画作陆续完成，我也给他们看了。

167
00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:59.390
And that went all the way up to like a couple of weeks ago, we got prototypes of the toys
这一直持续到几周前，我们收到了玩具的原型，

168
00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.170
and I gave them to the girls.
我把它们给了女儿们。

169
00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.370
And it was amazing.
这太棒了。

170
00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.270
They were like, oh, my God, this is amazing.
她们说，天哪，这太神奇了。

171
00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:06.890
And I said, what would you change?
我问，你们想改哪里吗？

172
00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.870
And they were like, his belly could be a little softer when I hug him.
她们说，我抱他的时候，他的肚子可以再软一点。

173
00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:12.510
And I was like, OK, good note.
我说，好的，很好的建议。

174
00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.870
And sure enough, they changed the toys and stuff.
果然，他们真的修改了玩具之类的东西。

175
00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.330
So it's been a family process.
所以这是一个家庭共同参与的过程。

176
00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.870
However, they have not seen the movie yet.
不过，她们还没看过这部电影。

177
00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:19.870
And I'll be honest with you.
老实说，

178
00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:24.610
I have never been more terrified to show two people anything in my life.
我这辈子从来没有像现在这样，给两个人看东西时感到如此紧张。

179
00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:29.990
This is the absolute sweetest thing that it was a family thing.
这绝对是最甜蜜的事情，因为它是一项家庭活动。

180
00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:33.610
And I just I know what that's like when your kids are old enough and you can kind of try
我明白当孩子们长大到一定程度，你可以尝试

181
00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:37.070
to you get to share your what you do with your kids.
与他们分享你的工作是什么感觉。

182
00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:37.930
Yeah.
是啊。

183
00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.330
Well, I'm in that magic window.
嗯，我正处于那个神奇的窗口期。

184
00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:42.970
They're in the perfect age right now where they're going to care.
她们现在正处于完美的年龄，会对此感兴趣。

185
00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.610
And I knew that if I did a movie for them in like three or four years, they'd be like,
我知道如果我三四年后再为她们拍电影，她们会说，

186
00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:48.030
oh, please stop.
噢，求你了，停下吧。

187
00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:51.210
Stop trying to stop trying to beg for our attention.
别再试图博取我们的关注了。

188
00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.070
So I just thought this is the magic window and it's great.
所以我认为这就是那个神奇的窗口期，感觉棒极了。

189
00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.870
And so we're doing a kind of a family premiere.
所以我们打算举办一场家庭首映礼。

190
00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.770
One of the main characters is purple.
其中一个主要角色是紫色的。

191
00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.590
So we're doing like a purple carpet and everything.
所以我们准备了紫色地毯之类的东西。

192
00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.110
So we're doing this whole little family.
我们正在筹备整个家庭活动。

193
00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:04.070
Unfortunately, we're pretending it's the premiere.
不幸的是，我们假装这就是首映礼。

194
00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.970
And I keep saying, don't tell them it's not the real premiere, please.
我一直说，千万别告诉她们这不是真正的首映礼，拜托了。

195
00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:07.730
Right, right.
对，没错。

196
00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.770
Luckily, they'll never know because this isn't in public.
幸运的是，她们永远不会知道，因为这不是公开的。

197
00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:10.410
So that's fine.
所以没关系。

198
00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:14.750
John, did you have an imaginary friend growing up?
约翰，你小时候有幻想朋友吗？

199
00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:16.830
I did have an imaginary friend.
我确实有一个幻想朋友。

200
00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:18.810
I had this imaginary friend.
我曾经有过这个幻想朋友。

201
00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:23.890
And it's so funny because only in talking about my imaginary friend in an interview did I realize
这真的很有趣，因为只有在采访中谈到我的幻想朋友时，我才意识到

202
00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:26.550
that he might be the one who's directing all the movies.
他可能就是那个执导所有电影的人。

203
00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.430
Because his name was Sam Brace.
因为他的名字叫山姆·布雷斯（Sam Brace）。

204
00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:32.910
My brother had braces at the time and I thought they were the cooleSt.
我哥哥当时戴着牙套，我觉得那酷毙了。

205
00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:36.370
I would find out eight years later, they were not the cooleSt.
八年后我才发现，那一点也不酷。

206
00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:40.650
But for a minute there, braces were the thing in my world.
但在那一小会儿，牙套就是我世界里最潮的东西。

207
00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.210
So his name was Sam Brace.
所以他的名字叫山姆·布雷斯。

208
00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:46.590
And he and I would go to the video store, which was like six blocks away or eight blocks away.
我和他会去录像带租赁店，大概离这儿六个或八个街区远。

209
00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:51.950
And so Sam Brace and I would walk to the video store to pick out a movie enacting that movie.
我和山姆·布雷斯会步行去店里挑一部电影，然后演出来。

210
00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:56.530
So we did action movies, horror movies, because I was too scared to watch horror movies.
我们演过动作片、恐怖片，因为我胆子小，不敢看恐怖片。

211
00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:57.390
So I just pretended.
所以我只是假装在看。

212
00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:01.050
And we just went with Werewolf, which was sort of the de facto scary thing.
我们选了《狼人》，那算是当时公认的恐怖片代表。

213
00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.430
And we ran away from werewolves.
我们假装从狼人身边逃跑。

214
00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:09.430
We were in action scenes and we're back to back as we saw on movie posters, just having each other's back.
我们演动作戏时会像电影海报上那样背靠背，互相掩护。

215
00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:10.190
That's what we did.
我们就是这么玩的。

216
00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:12.050
Aw, Sam's great.
噢，山姆真是太棒了。

217
00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.150
I love Sam.
我爱山姆。

218
00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:13.910
Sam Braces.
山姆·布雷斯。

219
00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:14.210
Sam is great.
山姆很棒。

220
00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:15.970
Braces were the coolest thing.
牙套曾经是最酷的东西。

221
00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:21.610
I remember my friend had a retainer and I took a paperclip and I unwrapped it and put it on my...
我记得我朋友戴过保持器，我就拿了个回形针拆开，戴在我的……

222
00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:22.130
What?
什么？

223
00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:22.790
Why?
为什么？

224
00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:23.650
I wore a paperclip.
我戴过回形针。

225
00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:24.010
Also did it.
我也干过。

226
00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.050
I also did that.
我也做过那种事。

227
00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:25.410
Yeah.
是啊。

228
00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:26.310
I did that too.
我也做过。

229
00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:32.210
Turns out retainers don't have that weird metal taste that makes you sick, but paperclips do.
结果发现保持器没有那种让人恶心的奇怪金属味，但回形针有。

230
00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:35.090
And they poke you in the guMs.
而且它们会扎到牙龈。

231
00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.290
We are so tickled that you're working with Steve Carell again.
我们很高兴看到你再次与史蒂夫·卡瑞尔合作。

232
00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:39.470
Steve plays the character.
史蒂夫饰演那个角色。

233
00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:39.770
Who's that?
那是谁？

234
00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:43.550
Steve Carell.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

235
00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.750
Steve Carell.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

236
00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.590
Oh, Steve's Carol.
噢，史蒂夫是卡罗尔（Carol）。

237
00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:47.170
Steve's Carol.
史蒂夫是卡罗尔。

238
00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.330
Yeah, that's the ice cream store in the world.
对，那是世界上最好的冰淇淋店。

239
00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:48.630
Yeah.
是啊。

240
00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:50.770
And he plays the character Blue.
他在片中饰演“蓝”这个角色。

241
00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:55.450
Can you tell us what it was like to work with Steve again after all those years?
能告诉我们时隔多年再次与史蒂夫合作是什么感觉吗？

242
00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:55.640
Oh my God.
天哪。

243
00:09:55.810 --> 00:10:01.290
Well, first of all, I wrote it with him in mind, which was really amazing because clearly as an actor,
首先，我在写剧本时就想到了他，这真的很棒，因为作为演员，他显然是天赋异禀。

244
00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.610
he's as talented as it comes.
他才华横溢。

245
00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.790
I think he's the funniest person I've ever met in my life.
我觉得他是我这辈子见过最幽默的人。

246
00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:08.450
So that wasn't hard to write for him, but it was also weird.
所以为他写剧本并不难，但感觉也很奇妙。

247
00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:14.390
I would laugh extra hard while writing thinking of like my friend Steve saying these things.
我在写的时候会笑得特别大声，想到我的朋友史蒂夫说这些台词的样子。

248
00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:17.350
And then it would immediately bring me back to the set of The Office.
这会立刻把我带回《办公室》的片场。

249
00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:22.890
And I would remember deliveries of not only his lines in the show, but lines off camera,
我会想起他不仅在剧中的台词，还有镜头外的那些台词，

250
00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:24.210
like bits that he would do.
比如他会即兴表演的那些梗。

251
00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.570
And I was like, oh my God, he's going to be great in this moment, blah, blah, blah.
当时我就想，天哪，他在这场戏里肯定会表现得非常棒，诸如此类的。

252
00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.230
Had no idea that he was going to do it.
我完全没想到他真的会那么做。

253
00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:32.490
And so, you know, when you asked me what it was like to work with him, I think in my head,
所以，你知道，当你问我跟他合作是什么感觉时，我脑子里想的是，

254
00:10:32.510 --> 00:10:34.130
I thought it's going to be just like The Office.
我以为会像《办公室》那样。

255
00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.030
It's going to be a laugh a minute.
肯定会每分钟都让人捧腹大笑。

256
00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.770
And the dude walks in.
结果那家伙走进来的时候。

257
00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:41.050
We had this video that we put out last week of him actually walking in, which was adorable.
我们上周发布了一段他真正走进来时的视频，非常可爱。

258
00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:47.650
But then as soon as we started working, instead of I had this huge grin on my face and tears were coming out of my eyes
但当我们真正开始工作时，我本以为自己会咧着嘴笑，结果却泪流满面，

259
00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:54.350
because he went into this whole speech about how proud he is of me and how he's watched everything I've directed
因为他开始长篇大论地说他有多为我感到骄傲，说他看过我执导的所有作品，

260
00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:58.170
and that he couldn't be more proud and he feels like a brother.
说他感到无比自豪，觉得我就像他的兄弟一样。

261
00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:06.410
And I was like, so the first day that I thought I'd be laughing my head off, I was just reaching for tissues, all of that.
当时我就想，第一天我本以为会笑得前仰后合，结果却一直在找纸巾擦眼泪，就是那种感觉。

262
00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:09.190
He was so unbelievably sweet and kind.
他真的难以置信地贴心和友善。

263
00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.830
And then he was nice about the script and everything.
而且他对剧本什么的也都评价得很好。

264
00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:16.370
And kind of as I was saying, the movie is not just a zany kind of movie about imaginary friends.
就像我刚才说的，这部电影不仅仅是一部关于幻想朋友的滑稽电影。

265
00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:19.830
It's about coping and getting through, you know, difficult times.
它还关乎如何应对和度过那些艰难时刻。

266
00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.730
And who do you turn to for that and stuff?
以及在那种时候你会向谁求助之类的。

267
00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:25.850
And he was just so into the idea of it and he was just so excited to be a part of it.
他非常认同这个理念，也对能参与其中感到非常兴奋。

268
00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:30.650
So it was my short answer long is it was one of the greatest things ever.
所以长话短说，这绝对是我经历过最棒的事情之一。

269
00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.490
And it was so much fun to see him again.
能再次见到他真的太开心了。

270
00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.950
I realized I hadn't seen him in years physically.
我意识到我已经好几年没在现实中见过他了。

271
00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:40.330
I mean, we had done that thing during COVID too on Some Good News, but that's the last time I had really seen him.
我是说，我们在疫情期间也一起做过《Some Good News》，但那是我最后一次真正见到他。

272
00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:42.910
And then he was so hilarious.
而且他当时真的太搞笑了。

273
00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:49.350
But I will say, fun story, the last day we recorded him, I secretly told the lead girl,
不过我要说个有趣的故事，在他录音的最后一天，我偷偷告诉了女主角，

274
00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:52.910
who is one of the most talented people you will ever meet in your life, her name's Kaylee Fleming.
她是我这辈子见过最有天赋的人之一，她叫凯莉·弗莱明。

275
00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:59.150
And Kaylee waits till the last week of shooting this movie, which was something like 55 days or something.
凯莉一直等到电影拍摄的最后一周，大概是第55天左右的时候。

276
00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:02.770
And she kept saying to me every night, I'm going to go home and have pizza.
她每天晚上都跟我说，我要回家吃披萨了。

277
00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.890
And I was like, wow, you just go home every night and have pizza.
我就说，哇，你每天晚上回家都吃披萨啊。

278
00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:05.990
I wish I could do that.
真希望我也能那样。

279
00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:09.710
And her mom finally goes, why don't you tell her what else do you do every night?
她妈妈终于忍不住说，你为什么不告诉她你每天晚上还干什么呢？

280
00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.210
And I said, what else do you do?
我说，你还干什么？

281
00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:14.710
And she goes, I eat pizza and I watch The Office.
她说，我吃着披萨看《办公室》。

282
00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:15.970
And I went, what's that?
我问，那是什么？

283
00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:20.830
She had not told me that she even knew what The Office was the entire time we knew each other.
我们认识这么久，她竟然一直没告诉我她知道《办公室》这部剧。

284
00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.850
And so then she finally says, I watch it every night.
最后她终于说，我每天晚上都看。

285
00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:24.790
It's one of my favorite shows.
那是我最喜欢的剧之一。

286
00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.790
She was so classy and cool about the whole thing.
她处理这件事的方式真是既优雅又酷。

287
00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:27.950
And I said, well, that's amazing.
我说，那太棒了。

288
00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:29.330
Do you want a selfie?
你想合影吗？

289
00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.390
And she went, no, I'm good.
她说，不用了，我挺好的。

290
00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:31.650
And it was...
当时就是……

291
00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:34.610
Oh my gosh, she's so cool.
天哪，她太酷了。

292
00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:36.030
She was so cool.
她真的太酷了。

293
00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.150
But then, of course, we took a selfie because I needed one.
但后来我们当然还是合影了，因为我需要一张。

294
00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:43.210
But then what I did was I overlapped Steve on her day to come in and do ADr.
然后我做了一件事，我把史蒂夫来做后期配音的时间安排在了她那天。

295
00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:47.810
And so she walked into the studio and saw Steve Carell and turned into duSt.
所以当她走进录音室看到史蒂夫·卡瑞尔时，整个人都惊呆了。

296
00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:51.870
She just went and turned into dust right in front of him, who was so adorable.
她就在他面前惊呆了，而他表现得非常可爱。

297
00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:53.990
And of course, he was so sweet.
当然，他依然非常贴心。

298
00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:55.310
And I don't know.
我也不知道该怎么说。

299
00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:57.490
I like watching people have their days made.
我喜欢看别人梦想成真的样子。

300
00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:58.330
It makes me smile.
这让我感到很开心。

301
00:12:58.630 --> 00:12:59.890
We know that about you.
我们了解你这一点。

302
00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:00.490
That's true.
确实如此。

303
