整个剧组进进出出那扇门大概有四次。

613
00:25:34.250 --> 00:25:38.370
And so we were out in the lobby waiting for him to call reset and we were laughing and
我们在大厅等着他喊重拍，我们还在那儿说笑，

614
00:25:38.370 --> 00:25:38.670
joking.
开玩笑。

615
00:25:39.130 --> 00:25:43.390
And when we came back in, I don't know how he did it, but he assembled the entirety of
当我们回来时，我不知道他是怎么做到的，但他召集了全体

616
00:25:43.390 --> 00:25:46.270
the crew and we can't, I'm like choking up just talking about it.
工作人员，我光是说起这件事就哽咽了。

617
00:25:46.330 --> 00:25:51.150
But then when you come back in and you see like your TV dad and all of your family waiting
但当你回来，看到你的“电视爸爸”和所有的家人都在那儿等着，

618
00:25:51.150 --> 00:25:53.250
there and clapping, and he said, that's the end of the office.
为你鼓掌，他说，这就是《办公室》的终点。

619
00:25:53.390 --> 00:25:58.350
And I, I think I black, I like, I think I like the color black came out of my mouth.
我当时，我想我断片了，我感觉，我想我嘴里都吐出黑色的东西了。

620
00:25:58.350 --> 00:26:04.570
Like I, it was just the scariest, most beautiful, horrific moment of my life.
就像，那是我一生中最可怕、最美好、最震撼的时刻。

621
00:26:04.730 --> 00:26:08.230
And then 30 minutes later, I took the Dunder Mifflin sign, which I think I've always lied
然后30分钟后，我拿走了邓德·米夫林（Dunder Mifflin）的招牌，我想我一直

622
00:26:08.230 --> 00:26:09.990
to Greg that I didn't take it, but I did.
对格雷格撒谎说我没拿，但我确实拿了。

623
00:26:10.810 --> 00:26:16.650
It's one of my favorite memories of our last day was watching you try to put it in the back
我最后一天最喜欢的记忆之一，就是看着你试图把它塞进

624
00:26:16.650 --> 00:26:17.250
of your car.
你的车后座。

625
00:26:17.970 --> 00:26:23.130
I was walking through the parking lot and I was like, oh, it's a Dunder Mifflin sign.
我当时正走过停车场，心想，哦，那是邓德·米夫林的招牌。

626
00:26:23.830 --> 00:26:24.170
Yeah.
是啊。

627
00:26:24.270 --> 00:26:25.450
And I was like, don't look over here.
我当时就想，别往这边看。

628
00:26:26.030 --> 00:26:27.070
Nothing's happening here.
这儿什么都没发生。

629
00:26:27.190 --> 00:26:28.670
It wasn't quite dark enough.
天色还不够暗。

630
00:26:28.790 --> 00:26:31.170
So it just looked like I was putting a body in a car.
所以看起来就像我在往车里塞一具尸体。

631
00:26:31.310 --> 00:26:37.610
And then I remember Greg came up to me at the end party and was like, Hey, um, we've
然后我记得杀青派对上格雷格走到我面前说，嘿，嗯，我们

632
00:26:37.610 --> 00:26:38.370
been looking for the sign.
一直在找那个招牌。

633
00:26:38.490 --> 00:26:39.190
Do you know where it is?
你知道它在哪吗？

634
00:26:39.270 --> 00:26:41.330
And I, it was literally like confessing to my dad.
我当时的感觉，简直就像在向我爸爸坦白一样。

635
00:26:41.330 --> 00:26:44.250
And I went, no, nope, no.
我说，没有，没，没有。

636
00:26:44.450 --> 00:26:46.150
And he goes, oh, that was the one thing I wanted.
他说，哦，那是我唯一想要的东西。

637
00:26:46.250 --> 00:26:48.190
And I was like, oh boy.
我当时心想，天哪。

638
00:26:48.510 --> 00:26:49.350
Oh God.
天哪。

639
00:26:51.210 --> 00:26:53.970
I never told anyone I saw you putting it in the car.
我从没告诉过任何人我看到你把它塞进车里。

640
00:26:54.370 --> 00:26:55.190
Well, now you did.
好吧，现在你说了。

641
00:26:55.390 --> 00:26:56.170
Now you told everyone.
现在你告诉所有人了。

642
00:26:56.950 --> 00:26:58.650
And I was dressed like a cat burglar.
而且我当时穿得像个入室窃贼一样。

643
00:27:00.570 --> 00:27:05.670
John, it's really funny to me because the moment that you would most wish to relive, just
约翰，这对我来说真的很有趣，因为你最想重温的时刻，仅仅是

644
00:27:05.670 --> 00:27:08.030
the moment of talking to the cast and crew.
和演职人员交谈的时刻。

645
00:27:08.030 --> 00:27:09.250
I know what you're going to say, Jenna.
我知道你要说什么，珍娜。

646
00:27:09.530 --> 00:27:10.770
I know what you're going to say.
我知道你要说什么。

647
00:27:11.230 --> 00:27:12.470
Is Rain's nightmare.
那是雷恩（Rainn）的噩梦。

648
00:27:13.090 --> 00:27:13.310
What?
什么？

649
00:27:13.710 --> 00:27:19.190
Do you remember when we were all sitting on set once and it was like a Tuesday and all
你还记得有一次我们都坐在片场，那是个周二，突然间

650
00:27:19.190 --> 00:27:24.330
of a sudden Rain out of nowhere, he bursts out and he goes, attention, attention.
雷恩毫无征兆地爆发了，他说，注意，注意。

651
00:27:24.330 --> 00:27:25.530
I need everyone's attention.
大家请注意。

652
00:27:25.690 --> 00:27:26.230
Listen to me.
听我说。

653
00:27:26.590 --> 00:27:31.110
From now on, we only ask, how was your weekend on Mondays?
从现在起，我们只在周一问“你周末过得怎么样？”

654
00:27:31.410 --> 00:27:36.330
You get one day, you get one day to ask me, how are you and how was your weekend?
你们只有一天，只有一天的时间来问我“你好吗”和“周末过得怎么样”。

655
00:27:36.470 --> 00:27:37.190
And then it's enough.
之后就够了。

656
00:27:37.370 --> 00:27:38.550
I can't take it anymore.
我实在受不了了。

657
00:27:38.550 --> 00:27:39.770
He like fractured.
他就像崩溃了一样。

658
00:27:39.950 --> 00:27:41.030
I can't take the questions anymore.
我再也受不了这些问题了。

659
00:27:41.410 --> 00:27:42.330
We were all like.
我们当时都觉得。

660
00:27:42.350 --> 00:27:44.310
It's like a Curb Your Enthusiasm episode.
就像《抑制热情》里的一集。

661
00:27:44.410 --> 00:27:44.790
It was.
确实是。

662
00:27:45.010 --> 00:27:45.250
What is happening?
到底发生了什么？

663
00:27:45.470 --> 00:27:49.150
And I remember Dale was right by him and he was like, jeez.
我记得戴尔当时就在他旁边，他说，天哪。

664
00:27:50.170 --> 00:27:52.470
And Rain fully talks about this.
雷恩完全谈论过这件事。

665
00:27:52.610 --> 00:27:54.010
We've had full conversations with him.
我们和他进行过深入的交谈。

666
00:27:54.090 --> 00:27:58.330
And he's like, remember that day I told everyone, don't ask me about the weekend on Tuesdays?
他说，还记得那天我告诉大家，周二别再问我周末的事了吗？

667
00:27:58.410 --> 00:27:59.910
It just like short-circuited.
就像短路了一样。

668
00:28:00.170 --> 00:28:00.220
Oh my God.
天哪。

669
00:28:00.510 --> 00:28:02.290
Rain would not want to revisit that.
雷恩肯定不想再重提那件事了。

670
00:28:02.410 --> 00:28:03.090
He would not.
他肯定不想。

671
00:28:03.090 --> 00:28:12.130
By the way, you know, another thing that you guys were both involved in was, I think, yeah, I think I said to Greg, do you mind if I make some sort of documentary about the end?
顺便说一下，你们俩都参与的另一件事是，我想，是的，我想我问过格雷格，介意我拍一部关于剧集终结的纪录片吗？

672
00:28:12.310 --> 00:28:13.670
And my buddy Danny shot it.
我朋友丹尼拍摄的。

673
00:28:13.830 --> 00:28:17.950
And I remember he showed me the rough cut of all of us saying goodbye to the office.
我记得他给我看了我们所有人向办公室告别的粗剪片段。

674
00:28:18.130 --> 00:28:22.510
And you guys all had the same reaction, which is, he was like, so what do you think about the end of the office?
你们当时的反应都一样，他问，你们对《办公室》的终结有什么看法？

675
00:28:22.510 --> 00:28:31.370
And you guys, both of you went, the end of the office, wow, it was just, we all couldn't even get past the first question.
你们俩都说，办公室的终结，哇，那简直……我们连第一个问题都回答不上来。

676
00:28:31.550 --> 00:28:32.210
It was too much.
那太沉重了。

677
00:28:32.390 --> 00:28:34.430
It was a beautiful, beautiful time.
那是一段非常、非常美好的时光。

678
00:28:34.450 --> 00:28:35.490
It really was.
确实是。

679
00:28:35.990 --> 00:28:36.890
It really was.
确实是。

680
00:28:36.970 --> 00:28:39.270
And you guys will have to live through that again, right?
你们还得再经历一次，对吧？

681
00:28:39.570 --> 00:28:40.250
Pretty soon.
很快了。

682
00:28:40.250 --> 00:28:41.370
In about 14 weeks or whatever.
大概14周后还是什么时候。

683
00:28:41.510 --> 00:28:41.670
Yeah.
是的。

684
00:28:42.430 --> 00:28:44.490
And you guys, are you going to run it back?
你们打算重来一遍吗？

685
00:28:44.610 --> 00:28:47.450
Are you just going to, like, people watch the show over and over?
你们只是打算，就像人们一遍又一遍地看这部剧那样？

686
00:28:47.450 --> 00:28:50.350
Why wouldn't you just do this again and find new things in episodes?
为什么不重做一遍，在剧集中发现新的东西呢？

687
00:28:50.510 --> 00:28:52.810
People are writing in and saying this to us, John.
人们写信告诉我们这件事，约翰。

688
00:28:53.090 --> 00:28:54.090
They're just like, do it again.
他们就是说，再做一次吧。

689
00:28:54.250 --> 00:28:54.630
I would.
我会的。

690
00:28:55.490 --> 00:28:56.270
Do it again.
再做一次。

691
00:28:56.310 --> 00:28:57.630
Let's talk about it in a different way.
让我们换个方式谈谈它。

692
00:28:58.230 --> 00:29:01.150
I mean, clearly Presentsky will tell the same story, so who cares?
我的意思是，显然普雷森斯基会讲同样的故事，所以谁在乎呢？

693
00:29:02.850 --> 00:29:04.110
This has been so much fun.
这真的太有趣了。

694
00:29:04.270 --> 00:29:04.830
So much fun.
太有趣了。

695
00:29:04.850 --> 00:29:05.350
Is it over already?
这就结束了吗？

696
00:29:05.510 --> 00:29:09.330
No, I'm going to bring us home with our call sheet questions that were on the back of the call sheet.
不，我要用通告单背面的问题来收尾。

697
00:29:09.690 --> 00:29:10.850
God, I missed your accent.
天哪，我好怀念你的口音。

698
00:29:11.230 --> 00:29:12.870
I'm going to bring it home with my lid.
我要用我的方式来收尾。

699
00:29:13.810 --> 00:29:14.170
Sorry.
抱歉。

700
00:29:14.590 --> 00:29:17.030
Both of my sisters from Texas are here visiting.
我两个来自德克萨斯州的姐妹正在这儿探亲。

701
00:29:18.110 --> 00:29:19.570
Oh, I can tell.
噢，我看得出来。

702
00:29:19.710 --> 00:29:20.390
Yes, I know.
是的，我知道。

703
00:29:20.510 --> 00:29:21.570
They've been here a few days.
他们已经在这儿待了几天了。

704
00:29:22.370 --> 00:29:23.390
Here we go.
开始了。

705
00:29:23.530 --> 00:29:24.810
The call sheet questions.
通告单上的问题。

706
00:29:25.510 --> 00:29:29.250
Number one, what was your first entertainment job?
第一个问题，你第一份演艺工作是什么？

707
00:29:30.430 --> 00:29:31.750
What does that entail?
那具体是做什么的？

708
00:29:31.890 --> 00:29:33.310
I think I was an extra.
我想我当时是个临时演员。

709
00:29:34.970 --> 00:29:41.070
Well, actually, I remember because my first job was an extra in a insurance commercial
嗯，其实我记得，因为我的第一份工作是在一个保险广告里当临时演员，

710
00:29:41.070 --> 00:29:46.710
that then they bumped me up to featured extra because I became the cashier.
后来他们把我升为特约演员，因为我成了收银员。

711
00:29:47.450 --> 00:29:51.010
And the only reason why I remember that so vividly is because the woman who was checking out,
我之所以记得那么清楚，是因为那个结账的女人，

712
00:29:51.130 --> 00:29:56.230
who was the lead of the commercial, was Margo Martindale, who I later was in a movie called
也就是广告的主角，是玛戈·马丁戴尔，后来我和她一起拍了一部电影叫

713
00:29:56.230 --> 00:29:57.430
The Hollers, and she played my mom.
《霍勒一家》，她在里面演我妈妈。

714
00:29:57.670 --> 00:29:59.090
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

715
00:29:59.770 --> 00:30:00.150
Yeah.
是啊。

716
00:30:00.370 --> 00:30:02.890
And then they gave me my SAG card that day.
然后那天他们给了我演员工会卡。

717
00:30:03.270 --> 00:30:06.370
And I remember her saying something to the effect of like, yeah, you better.
我记得她说了一些类似的话，比如，没错，你最好拿着。

718
00:30:06.750 --> 00:30:07.290
That's right.
没错。

719
00:30:07.370 --> 00:30:09.610
You will give it to him because he's doing great.
你会把它给他的，因为他表现得很棒。

720
00:30:09.790 --> 00:30:10.850
I think you're doing great.
我觉得你表现得很棒。

721
00:30:10.850 --> 00:30:12.210
And I was like, oh, my God.
当时我就想，天哪。

722
00:30:13.230 --> 00:30:17.030
Did you guys talk about that story when you did the movie together?
你们一起拍电影的时候聊过这个故事吗？

723
00:30:17.750 --> 00:30:18.490
Oh, yeah.
噢，聊过。

724
00:30:18.830 --> 00:30:21.670
I think she probably had something to do with getting me my SAG card.
我觉得她可能在帮我拿到演员工会卡这件事上出了力。

725
00:30:21.870 --> 00:30:26.070
So, yeah, she is the most wonderful, wonderful.
所以，没错，她真是太棒了，太棒了。

726
00:30:26.430 --> 00:30:27.450
Have you guys worked with her?
你们和她合作过吗？

727
00:30:27.670 --> 00:30:28.510
I have not.
我没有。

728
00:30:28.770 --> 00:30:29.630
No, big fan.
没有，我是她的超级粉丝。

729
00:30:29.890 --> 00:30:30.430
Big fan.
超级粉丝。

730
00:30:30.690 --> 00:30:32.430
Would probably not be cool around her.
在她面前我可能没法保持冷静。

731
00:30:32.510 --> 00:30:32.560
Get there quick.
快去见见她吧。

732
00:30:32.770 --> 00:30:33.250
Would try.
我会试着去。

733
00:30:34.490 --> 00:30:36.170
Okay, number two.
好的，第二个问题。

734
00:30:36.510 --> 00:30:38.550
Do you play a musical instrument?
你会演奏乐器吗？

735
00:30:39.090 --> 00:30:40.910
I did play a musical instrument.
我曾经会演奏乐器。

736
00:30:41.090 --> 00:30:46.610
I played trumpet for nine years and probably could not do that at all right now.
我吹了九年小号，但现在可能完全吹不了了。

737
00:30:46.810 --> 00:30:47.710
My lips would fall off.
我的嘴唇会受不了的。

738
00:30:47.850 --> 00:30:53.630
But I have been desperately trying to learn piano and guitar, and it's going on 15 years now.
但我一直拼命想学钢琴和吉他，到现在都快15年了。

739
00:30:53.750 --> 00:30:55.870
So I can play Let It Be.
所以我能弹《Let It Be》。

740
00:30:55.870 --> 00:30:58.890
I remember you had a beautiful little upright piano, remember?
我记得你有一架漂亮的小立式钢琴，记得吗？

741
00:30:59.210 --> 00:30:59.430
That's right.
没错。

742
00:30:59.570 --> 00:31:01.050
And I felt like you played it really well.
我觉得你弹得很好。

743
00:31:01.050 --> 00:31:02.050
So maybe it's more than 15.
所以可能不止15年了。

744
00:31:02.230 --> 00:31:02.750
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

745
00:31:04.170 --> 00:31:06.070
Can you play any song?
你会弹什么歌吗？

746
00:31:06.730 --> 00:31:09.670
Yes, I can play some Beatles stuff.
会，我会弹一些披头士的歌。

747
00:31:09.830 --> 00:31:12.790
I can play that amazing Stay.
我会弹那首很棒的《Stay》。

748
00:31:13.570 --> 00:31:14.030
Brianna.
布里安娜。

749
00:31:14.210 --> 00:31:15.210
Brianna sings Stay.
布里安娜唱《Stay》。

750
00:31:15.350 --> 00:31:16.650
Yeah, they make me happy.
是啊，它们让我感到快乐。

751
00:31:17.030 --> 00:31:18.090
I love it.
我喜欢。

752
00:31:18.550 --> 00:31:19.530
Okay, number three.
好，第三个问题。

753
00:31:19.770 --> 00:31:23.210
What's a place you've been to that you absolutely loved?
你去过的地方里，哪个是你绝对最喜欢的？

754
00:31:23.650 --> 00:31:24.570
Oh, man.
天哪。

755
00:31:24.970 --> 00:31:25.890
So many.
太多了。

756
00:31:26.090 --> 00:31:31.110
I've been so lucky in the last couple of years on Jack Ryan to travel all these different wild
过去几年拍《杰克·莱恩》时，我有幸去了很多不同的狂野

757
00:31:31.110 --> 00:31:31.470
places.
地方。

758
00:31:31.470 --> 00:31:36.570
But I got to say something about Paris has stolen a piece of my heart forever.
但我得说，巴黎以某种方式永远偷走了我的一部分心。

759
00:31:36.830 --> 00:31:41.090
There's something about it where when I close my eyes, I feel like it's still in the 1920s.
它有一种魔力，当我闭上眼睛，感觉就像回到了20世纪20年代。

760
00:31:41.190 --> 00:31:42.970
And I'm just hearing jazz for the first time.
我仿佛第一次听到了爵士乐。

761
00:31:43.130 --> 00:31:45.330
And like all these epic writers are walking the streets.
感觉那些伟大的作家们正走在街上。

762
00:31:45.330 --> 00:31:48.830
And I did a very nerdy thing in Paris, which I highly recommend.
我在巴黎做了一件非常书呆子的事，我强烈推荐大家也试试。

763
00:31:49.250 --> 00:31:53.530
I read Immovable Feast at the same cafes that Hemingway wrote them at.
我在海明威写书的那些咖啡馆里读了《流动的盛宴》。

764
00:31:53.790 --> 00:31:55.590
And it was full nerdville.
简直是书呆子天堂。

765
00:31:55.790 --> 00:31:56.990
I had the best time ever.
我玩得开心极了。

766
00:31:56.990 --> 00:32:01.850
John, I read Immovable Feast because you told me how much you loved it.
约翰，我读《流动的盛宴》是因为你告诉我你有多喜欢它。

767
00:32:02.230 --> 00:32:03.610
I've never told you that.
我从没跟你说过。

768
00:32:03.650 --> 00:32:05.410
I thought, oh, my God.
我当时心想，天哪。

769
00:32:05.830 --> 00:32:08.970
Years ago, you were like, oh, Immovable Feast is so good.
几年前，你说过《流动的盛宴》太棒了。

770
00:32:09.110 --> 00:32:11.110
So I went and got it and I'd never read it.
所以我去买了它，但我之前从没读过。

771
00:32:11.270 --> 00:32:15.350
I still have the paperback on my nightstand, like in my stack of favorite books.
那本平装书现在还放在我的床头柜上，就在我最喜欢的书堆里。

772
00:32:15.770 --> 00:32:18.610
And it's so amazing.
它真的太棒了。

773
00:32:18.790 --> 00:32:20.090
But I've never told you that.
但我从没跟你说过。

774
00:32:20.310 --> 00:32:21.250
Yes, it's so good.
没错，它真的很好。

775
00:32:21.250 --> 00:32:22.170
Oh, my God.
天哪。

776
00:32:22.610 --> 00:32:27.130
OK, next question is, what do you like to do on the weekends?
好，下一个问题，你周末喜欢做什么？

777
00:32:27.950 --> 00:32:28.910
Anything with my kids.
和孩子们在一起做什么都行。

778
00:32:29.110 --> 00:32:31.230
Honestly, it's just it's so much fun.
老实说，那真的太有趣了。

779
00:32:31.350 --> 00:32:34.290
And I've been shooting in London recently and flying back on the weekends to see them.
我最近一直在伦敦拍戏，周末会飞回来见他们。

780
00:32:34.670 --> 00:32:41.250
And so as soon as I get back, it's just like I said, it sounds like I'm still promoting the movie, but it's true.
所以只要我一回来，就像我说的，听起来好像我还在宣传电影，但这是真的。

781
00:32:41.390 --> 00:32:47.670
Like anything to get around their imagination or be dressed up in something or have my makeup done and hair done.
比如陪他们发挥想象力，或者穿上奇装异服，或者让他们给我化妆做头发。

782
00:32:48.370 --> 00:32:49.910
That's the perfect day for me.
那对我来说就是完美的一天。

783
00:32:51.250 --> 00:32:52.870
OK, don't cry.
好了，别哭。

784
00:32:53.310 --> 00:32:57.690
Number five, what is your favorite midnight snack?
第五个问题，你最喜欢的宵夜是什么？

785
00:32:58.570 --> 00:32:59.730
Oh, that's tough.
噢，这很难选。

786
00:33:00.450 --> 00:33:02.570
Mine's a sliding scale because it's leftovers.
我的宵夜是浮动的，因为通常是剩菜。

787
00:33:03.030 --> 00:33:04.130
I'm a huge.
我是个超级剩菜爱好者。

788
00:33:04.650 --> 00:33:09.630
There's something about the refrigerator that makes whatever meal was made.
冰箱有一种魔力，能让任何做好的饭菜——

789
00:33:09.910 --> 00:33:10.850
Definitely not by me.
当然不是我做的——

790
00:33:11.490 --> 00:33:11.710
Better.
变得更好吃。

791
00:33:12.190 --> 00:33:19.650
And I will say I have I have Emily's blessing on that, especially any like bolognese or stew or something like that.
我得说，我有艾米丽的许可，尤其是像肉酱面、炖菜之类的东西。

792
00:33:19.650 --> 00:33:22.390
It just gets better and better just sitting in the refrigerator.
它们在冰箱里放着只会越来越入味。

793
00:33:22.590 --> 00:33:29.690
So I'm I'm a leftovers guy and usually a two or three portion or guy like, oh, I'll just have one more.
所以我是个剩菜党，通常会吃两三份，心想，噢，我再吃一份就好。

794
00:33:30.750 --> 00:33:34.090
You say that you don't cook, but do you have a go to meal?
你说你不做饭，但你有拿手菜吗？

795
00:33:34.230 --> 00:33:37.370
Like, do you have if you had to cook for an occasion?
比如，如果必须为某个场合下厨的话？

796
00:33:37.650 --> 00:33:41.190
Do you have a thing like I feel like everybody has one one meal, right?
你有没有那种——我觉得每个人都有一道拿手菜，对吧？

797
00:33:41.550 --> 00:33:42.750
Have I not told you the story?
我没跟你讲过那个故事吗？

798
00:33:42.750 --> 00:33:47.910
It was Mother's Day and it was my gift to my wife, which makes me sound like guess what I did.
那是母亲节，是我送给妻子的礼物，这听起来让我显得……你猜我做了什么。

799
00:33:48.090 --> 00:33:49.170
It's just that's stupid.
那简直太蠢了。

800
00:33:49.450 --> 00:33:50.870
But we actually had a bet.
但我们其实打了个赌。

801
00:33:50.990 --> 00:33:51.630
This is a true story.
这是一个真实的故事。

802
00:33:52.050 --> 00:33:54.510
We had a bet that Leonardo DiCaprio.
我们打了个赌，关于莱昂纳多·迪卡普里奥。

803
00:33:54.750 --> 00:34:01.590
I said he was younger than me because I said that cherubic face could not be as old as I am, which is dirt.
我说他比我年轻，因为我觉得那张娃娃脸不可能像我一样老，我都老掉牙了。

804
00:34:01.910 --> 00:34:04.690
And she said he's definitely a couple of years older than you.
她说他绝对比你大几岁。

805
00:34:04.710 --> 00:34:05.330
That's not true.
那不是真的。

806
00:34:05.470 --> 00:34:06.150
And I said, I'll bet.
我说，那我们打赌吧。

807
00:34:06.270 --> 00:34:06.870
She goes, how about this?
她说，赌什么呢？

808
00:34:06.950 --> 00:34:07.590
If you win?
如果你赢了呢？

809
00:34:07.790 --> 00:34:09.010
I forget what hers was.
我忘了她赌的是什么了。

810
00:34:09.010 --> 00:34:12.250
I think back in the day, it was like, you could play Call of Duty for one full day.
我想在当时，大概是你可以玩一整天的《使命召唤》之类的。

811
00:34:12.370 --> 00:34:14.230
How nerdy that I was like, yeah, yeah.
我当时居然说“好啊好啊”，真是个书呆子。

812
00:34:15.410 --> 00:34:20.090
And then she said, and if you lose, you have to cook me my first meal.
然后她说，如果你输了，你就得给我做第一顿饭。

813
00:34:20.250 --> 00:34:20.890
And I said, fine.
我说，行。

814
00:34:21.250 --> 00:34:23.710
And so I lost, which is, I still can't believe it.
结果我输了，到现在我都不敢相信。

815
00:34:23.970 --> 00:34:25.750
Leo, you're 18 in my book.
莱奥，在我心里你才18岁。

816
00:34:26.010 --> 00:34:30.270
So the first meal I cooked became one of my old standbys, which is cocaven.
所以我做的第一顿饭成了我的拿手菜之一，也就是红酒炖鸡。

817
00:34:30.930 --> 00:34:31.330
Cocaven.
红酒炖鸡？

818
00:34:31.330 --> 00:34:31.630
What?
什么？

819
00:34:32.550 --> 00:34:32.810
Yeah.
对啊。

820
00:34:33.770 --> 00:34:36.190
Just cocaven is your meal?
你做的第一顿饭竟然是红酒炖鸡？

821
00:34:36.190 --> 00:34:39.030
I mean, I thought you were going to say I made meatloaf.
我还以为你会说你做了肉饼之类的。

822
00:34:39.170 --> 00:34:39.510
Nope.
并没有。

823
00:34:39.990 --> 00:34:40.330
Wow.
哇。

824
00:34:40.770 --> 00:34:42.670
No, this is my plug for Ina.
不，这是我给伊娜打的广告。

825
00:34:42.830 --> 00:34:46.690
I just went straight to you because I know Em's a huge fan of Ina's.
我直接去找了你，因为我知道艾姆是伊娜的超级粉丝。

826
00:34:46.790 --> 00:34:52.570
So I went straight to her book and opened some pages of, and I was like, what do I get after
所以我直接翻开她的书，看了几页，心想我该从哪里开始呢？

827
00:34:52.570 --> 00:34:52.850
here?
这里？

828
00:34:52.990 --> 00:34:56.450
And I wanted to impress her because it was the first time I was going to cook her anything
我想给她留下深刻印象，因为那是我第一次给她做饭，

829
00:34:56.450 --> 00:34:58.450
that wasn't like grilled cheese or scrambled eggs.
而不是烤奶酪三明治或炒鸡蛋之类的。

830
00:34:58.650 --> 00:34:58.990
Sure.
当然。

831
00:34:59.090 --> 00:35:02.350
So I went full cocaven and I said, you have to be really honeSt.
所以我全力以赴做了红酒炖鸡，我说，你一定要诚实评价。

832
00:35:02.570 --> 00:35:04.710
And she said, it's fantastic.
她说，太棒了。

833
00:35:04.730 --> 00:35:05.590
Keep making it.
继续做这个。

834
00:35:05.590 --> 00:35:07.030
So now it's one of my standbys.
所以现在它成了我的拿手菜之一。

835
00:35:07.210 --> 00:35:08.070
That's amazing.
太厉害了。

836
00:35:08.250 --> 00:35:08.810
That's impressive.
令人印象深刻。

837
00:35:09.030 --> 00:35:10.170
I'm happy to cook it for you guys.
我很乐意为你们做这道菜。

838
00:35:10.330 --> 00:35:11.110
We'll eat it.
我们会吃的。

839
00:35:11.750 --> 00:35:12.510
Ina's the go-to.
伊娜是首选。

840
00:35:12.790 --> 00:35:14.190
Ina is the go-to.
伊娜就是首选。

841
00:35:14.390 --> 00:35:17.870
Every Christmas morning, we have to have Ina Gartens.
每个圣诞节早晨，我们都必须吃伊娜·加滕的食谱。

842
00:35:18.130 --> 00:35:21.830
It's like a raspberry crumble thing.
那是一种覆盆子酥皮点心。

843
00:35:22.190 --> 00:35:26.230
For the listeners who can't see, Jenna's fingers are moving, which means we're almost there.
对于看不到画面的听众，珍娜的手指正在动，这意味着我们快做好了。

844
00:35:27.630 --> 00:35:28.910
We're crumbling it.
我们在弄碎它。

845
00:35:28.990 --> 00:35:32.370
We're crumbling the pastry in our fingers is what's happening.
我们正在用手指捏碎酥皮，就是这样。

846
00:35:34.290 --> 00:35:41.090
Well, guys, I married a baker, so, you know, none of my pants fit me anymore.
伙计们，我嫁给了一个烘焙师，所以，你们懂的，我的裤子没一条能穿得上了。

847
00:35:41.390 --> 00:35:42.170
Oh, my God.
天哪。

848
00:35:42.330 --> 00:35:44.450
But I do eat some delicious food.
但我确实吃到了美味的食物。

849
00:35:44.570 --> 00:35:45.390
It is a wonderful thing.
这是一件美妙的事情。

850
00:35:45.390 --> 00:35:49.110
I will say, I love your Instagram when you show the baked goods and the things that you
我得说，我很喜欢你在Instagram上展示烘焙食品和那些你做的东西。

851
00:35:49.110 --> 00:35:50.170
guys have eaten together.
你们一起吃过饭了。

852
00:35:50.470 --> 00:35:51.770
It's a problem for me.
这对我来说是个问题。

853
00:35:52.130 --> 00:35:52.570
It's a problem.
这是个问题。

854
00:35:52.690 --> 00:35:54.710
No, it's, I mean, that's fantastic.
不，我是说，那太棒了。

855
00:35:54.970 --> 00:35:55.550
But it's great.
但这很棒。

856
00:35:55.550 --> 00:35:58.050
Well, then she drives the leftovers over to my house.
好吧，然后她会开车把剩菜送到我家。

857
00:35:58.090 --> 00:35:58.370
I do.
我确实会。

858
00:35:58.530 --> 00:35:59.650
Like, to get them out of her house.
就像是，为了把它们从她家清出去一样。

859
00:35:59.770 --> 00:36:00.930
I've got to get them out.
我必须把它们清出去。

860
00:36:00.930 --> 00:36:05.630
She says, you drive it over as if it's like a trailer that takes that many baked goods.
她说，你开车送过去的样子，就好像那是装载那么多烘焙食品的拖车一样。

861
00:36:05.890 --> 00:36:07.050
But it is a little bit.
但确实有点像。

862
00:36:07.170 --> 00:36:09.470
She's like, here's seven dozen lemon drop cookies.
她会说，给你七打柠檬糖霜饼干。

863
00:36:09.490 --> 00:36:10.290
I have to tell you.
我得告诉你。

864
00:36:10.290 --> 00:36:11.090
I want them out of my house.
我想把它们从我家清出去。

865
00:36:11.270 --> 00:36:15.550
If you live within driving distance of me, chances are I've left you baked goods on your
如果你住在我开车能到的范围内，很有可能我已经在你的门廊上放了烘焙食品。

866
00:36:15.550 --> 00:36:15.930
porch.
门廊。

867
00:36:16.050 --> 00:36:17.750
Like, so many people are like, Ange, what is this?
很多人会问，安吉，这是什么？

868
00:36:17.830 --> 00:36:18.730
I'm like, just take it.
我就说，拿着就是了。

869
00:36:19.470 --> 00:36:22.250
You just throw cookies at people as they're walking their dog?
你就是在那儿给遛狗的人扔饼干？

870
00:36:22.470 --> 00:36:22.990
She does.
她确实会这样。

871
00:36:23.290 --> 00:36:23.650
Take it.
拿着。

872
00:36:25.820 --> 00:36:28.760
Oh, John, it's been so fun to reconnect with you.
噢，约翰，能和你重新联系上真是太开心了。

873
00:36:28.940 --> 00:36:30.140
We're so excited for your movie.
我们对你的电影感到非常兴奋。

874
00:36:30.300 --> 00:36:33.140
Everybody, it comes out this Friday, May 17th.
各位，电影将于本周五，5月17日上映。

875
00:36:33.700 --> 00:36:36.200
Go, bring tissues, weep with us.
去吧，带上纸巾，和我们一起哭。

876
00:36:36.360 --> 00:36:38.780
Yes, we're going to share all about it in our Insta stories.
是的，我们会在我们的Instagram快拍里分享关于它的一切。

877
00:36:38.960 --> 00:36:41.360
We'll put swipe up so you can go find it.
我们会放上向上滑动的链接，这样你们就能找到它了。

878
00:36:41.880 --> 00:36:43.460
John, we're so happy for you.
约翰，我们真为你感到高兴。

879
00:36:43.820 --> 00:36:45.320
I don't even know how to swipe up.
我甚至不知道怎么向上滑动。

880
00:36:45.440 --> 00:36:47.040
So you guys are way ahead of me.
所以你们比我领先多了。

881
00:36:47.360 --> 00:36:48.040
Way ahead of you guys.
比你们领先多了。

882
00:36:48.240 --> 00:36:50.500
Honestly, I think I said this to you again in the COVID thing.
老实说，我觉得我在疫情期间又跟你说过一次。

883
00:36:50.800 --> 00:36:54.100
It brings me so much joy that you guys are doing this show.
看到你们做这个节目，我感到非常快乐。

884
00:36:54.100 --> 00:36:55.780
And that you guys are doing it together.
而且你们是在一起做这件事。

885
00:36:56.020 --> 00:36:59.220
And that you guys are seeming to have so much fun doing it.
而且看起来你们做得很开心。

886
00:36:59.340 --> 00:37:00.920
I mean, this is not a job for you.
我是说，这对你们来说不是一份工作。

887
00:37:00.980 --> 00:37:01.860
It is very obvious.
这显而易见。

888
00:37:02.480 --> 00:37:04.780
And boy, are you bringing joy to a lot of people.
天哪，你们确实给很多人带来了快乐。

889
00:37:04.920 --> 00:37:05.760
And I just, I love it.
我真的，我太喜欢了。

890
00:37:05.880 --> 00:37:07.620
Thank you for having me do this today.
谢谢你们今天邀请我来做这个。

891
00:37:07.740 --> 00:37:08.380
This is great.
这太棒了。

892
00:37:08.840 --> 00:37:09.560
Aw, John.
噢，约翰。

893
00:37:09.740 --> 00:37:13.060
Well, you know, working with my best friend brings me so much joy.
嗯，你知道，和最好的朋友一起工作给我带来了很多快乐。

894
00:37:13.280 --> 00:37:16.680
And then we get to reconnect and see you and air hug.
然后我们还能重新联系，见到你，来个隔空拥抱。

895
00:37:17.160 --> 00:37:18.800
Yes, air hugs, John.
是的，隔空拥抱，约翰。

896
00:37:19.180 --> 00:37:25.620
How fun was that?
那有多好玩？

897
00:37:25.620 --> 00:37:26.620
I just love him.
我真是太喜欢他了。

898
00:37:26.620 --> 00:37:28.000
And I'm so proud of him.
我为他感到骄傲。

899
00:37:28.100 --> 00:37:29.520
And I can't wait to see this movie.
我迫不及待想看这部电影了。

900
00:37:30.260 --> 00:37:30.940
Same, lady.
我也是，亲爱的。

901
00:37:31.360 --> 00:37:32.700
John, we love you.
约翰，我们爱你。

902
00:37:32.880 --> 00:37:34.280
We are here for you.
我们会一直支持你。

903
00:37:34.440 --> 00:37:36.260
Thanks for being on the podcast again.
感谢你再次来到我们的播客。

904
00:37:36.460 --> 00:37:37.520
And go check out If.
大家一定要去看《神秘友友》。

905
00:37:37.640 --> 00:37:40.600
It's in theaters this Friday, May 17th.
本周五，5月17日，影院上映。

906
00:37:40.840 --> 00:37:41.720
See you next week.
下周见。

907
00:37:41.900 --> 00:37:43.120
See you next week.
下周见。

908
00:37:46.090 --> 00:37:48.130
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

909
00:37:48.450 --> 00:37:52.530
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Earwolf、珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金赛制作。

910
00:37:52.730 --> 00:37:55.030
Our senior producer is Cassie Jerkins.
我们的高级制作人是凯西·杰金斯。

911
00:37:55.250 --> 00:37:57.310
Our audio engineer is Jordan Duffy.
我们的音频工程师是乔丹·达菲。

912
00:37:57.590 --> 00:37:59.790
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubaco.
我们的助理制作人是安斯利·布巴科。

913
00:37:59.790 --> 00:38:03.050
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿的《橡胶树》。

914
00:38:03.050 --> 00:38:03.430
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。
